	(text "C9: RUN runs over two headers to the\ntact switch on the front board; 100 nF\nagainst ESD / noise resets (module\npull-up is ~50k only)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 82.55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2d31510-ad33-401f-b083-235a96adfb87")
	)
	(text "VBUS (40): USB 5 V only, not used\nVSYS (39): supply from USB (via the module diode) or from the bus via D1\n3V3 (36): module regulator, feeds OLED, encoders, H11L1, MIDI OUT source"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 62.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4ac15d6c-d6bb-4e59-9f85-16725d3fbf07")
	)
	(text "unused GPIO left open:\nGP9, GP16-GP22, ADC_VREF"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.17 100.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "88df1fdb-73b5-44f7-9da0-193c1681be48")
	)
	(text "GP0/GP1 = UART0\nstdio (debug J7)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "547770e4-e5d0-4fb0-bd71-01da99eb167e")
	)
	(text "MIDI IN  (TRS type A on the panel: tip = DIN 5, ring = DIN 4, sleeve open)\nH11L1 output is open collector, idle high. Bus MIDI RX joins the same node through D3: idle high on both,\nwhichever pulls low wins (wired AND), no contention. R2 = 4k7 so each module loads the bus RX with only\n~0.6 mA (ten modules ~6 mA at the hub, low level ~0.5 V); BAT85 for its low Vf, capacitance and leakage.\nFirmware: gpio_disable_pulls(GP5) - the pad default pull-down would divide a 4k7 pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8366514c-7bce-4040-9610-4eb76d9df9a5")
	)
	(text "MIDI OUT at 3.3 V: 33R from +3V3 to DIN 4 (ring), 33R from UART1 TX to DIN 5 (tip), sleeve = GND at the jack.\nCA-033 specifies 33R (0.5 W, survives a pin-4 short) + 10R; 33/33 gives ~4.1 mA worst case into a 220R + LED receiver,\nsame class as PJRC's 47/47. Firmware: set GP4 drive strength to 12 mA (default 4 mA is below the loop current)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 93.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d9954cba-b164-45b5-a669-50740c70739b")
	)
	(text "R17-R20: 100k"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "862831f7-d1d8-431b-90d5-007f151d1d4d")
	)
	(text "PCM5102A module (small purple GY-PCM5102): SCK to GND (internal PLL from BCK), VIN from VSYS (on-board LDOs).\nFLT/DEMP/XSMT/FMT are normally set by the solder bridges on the module back (H1L=L normal, H2L=L de-emphasis off,\nH3L=H un-mute, H4L=L I2S). R17-R20 (100k) pull them the same way from the module's own A3V3/GND, so an unbridged\nreplacement module still plays; a bridge always wins against 100k, so nothing can be shorted.\nOutputs: 470R + 2.2 nF on the module, then R15/R16 1k here - a mispatched +/-12 V Eurorack output is limited to\n~8 mA into the DAC clamps and a shorted plug stays above the 1k minimum load. 2.1 Vrms line level, no output stage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 189.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bf8fc7ae-4f96-4a8d-a6ac-e45393e8cba7")
	)
	(text "Bus 2: L / GND / R,\nin parallel with the front jacks"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 283.21 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b2265805-ff69-48b4-993c-9c8d48f687ad")
	)
	(text "Bus 1: 2x3 shrouded, 2.54 mm. 1/2 GND, 3/4 +5V, 5 GND, 6 MIDI RX (3.3 V logic from the hub).\nBus +5V feeds VSYS through D1 - never VBUS - so USB and bus power coexist (docs/MODULE_BUS.md).\nJ5, J6, D1, D3 can stay unpopulated on a module that never sees a bus; the footprints cost nothing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 279.4 38.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "920eaac0-e9c3-42df-baf7-a3426563dd27")
	)
	(text "J7: stdio (pico_enable_stdio_uart) - footprint only, DNP"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 59.69 199.39 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "52d0512c-432d-4f2d-be58-c354cb69476d")
	)
	(text "BOOT reaches the module at a pad on its underside -- it is on no\nheader pin. On a Pico 2 that is TP6; the pad sits behind the 1k to\nQSPI_SS_N, so the tact switch on the front board goes straight to it,\nno resistor of ours. Unbrickable module.\nTP2 is the landing pad for a spring pin, under TP6, 11.04 mm below it.\nTP1 is the fallback at the board edge: solder a wire instead. A\nWaveshare RP2350-Plus has its pad elsewhere and takes the wire."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a4735e62-6924-47ee-9b85-9e515628bfa7")
	)
	(text "J1 / J2: two 1x12 pin headers, 2.54 mm - they carry every signal to the front board and hold the boards parallel.\nThe mating sockets J3 / J4 sit on the front board with the same pin order."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300 205.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2b464996-f877-4055-9906-849ba1df37f6")
	)
	(text "Hierarchical labels are the board-to-board signals (SDA/SCL and AUDIO_L/R continue from local labels at A1/A3);\nMIDI_TX/RX, I2S_*, UART0_*, BUS_*, A3V3 stay on this board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300 209.55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ec6d5d0c-f029-4e54-b933-186bfae53857")
	)
	(text_box "Design notes\n- One board for all ten instruments; the pin map is core/include/project_config.h (GP2/3 I2C1, GP4/5 UART1, GP26-28 I2S, encoders GP6-8/10-15).\n- Power: USB into the module, or bus +5V -> D1 -> VSYS. Both may be present at once; the higher wins, nothing back-feeds the USB host.\n- MIDI IN is opto-isolated once here (H11L1); the bus MIDI RX is already logic level from the hub and joins through D3.\n- No output stage: 2.1 Vrms from the DAC module goes straight to the jacks and to bus 2. Mixer input must be high impedance (470R on the module).\n- Everything the enclosure dictates is off this board: encoders, display and the RUN/BOOT tact switches on the front board (sheet 3), jacks on the wired panel (sheet 4). Both boards 45 x 80 mm, 2 layers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 246.38 0)
		(size 220.98 20.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d0e5f1a-c93b-45b4-aaef-7c728c26f6a1")
	)
